(text "ESP32-WROOM-32D" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 20 0) (effects (font (size 2 2) (bold yes)) (justify left top)) (uuid "494cba9d-6a2d-4b50-bcc5-4d60ae67ae40"))
(text "EN: 10k + 1 uF delay (Espressif reference) so the chip starts only after 3.3 V is stable.\nQ201/Q202: the usual two-transistor auto-reset, so esptool can reset and enter the bootloader through\nDTR/RTS of a USB-serial adapter (same pin order as the old SV1 header). Strapping pins IO0/IO2/IO12/IO15\nare left free or pulled the safe way. Flash pins (SD0-SD3, CLK, CMD) must stay unconnected.\nDo not connect the adapter's 3.3 V while the battery is fitted (two regulators would fight)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 24 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "a06a95fd-f9a0-4e2c-bcb1-4e1ca0e663b5"))
